       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you're the attending and that you've confirmed it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily has no recognized therapeutic use. It's well above the 200 mg/day maximum, and the risk to the patient is serious. I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nYou still have other ways to get it done:\n- **Enter it yourself** in the order-entry system. That will trigger the dose-range hard stop and the pharmacist's review, which are the right checks for an order like this.\n- **Call pharmacy or clinical toxicology**, or the poison center at 1-800-222-1222, if there's an unusual reason for this dose.\n\nI'm glad to enter any dose up to 200 mg/day now. I can also enter a titration schedule, for example 50 mg, then 100 mg, then 150 mg, then 200 mg, with a note for monitoring."
